WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.833
- Your new book.

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:02.220
So, it's called "Making a Scene".

00:00:02.220 --> 00:00:03.720
So, why did you name it that?

00:00:03.720 --> 00:00:06.480
- Well, it sort of has two meanings.

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:08.670
One is about how art is really healing.

00:00:08.670 --> 00:00:10.680
And for me that has been acting

00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:12.540
and in acting you make scenes,

00:00:12.540 --> 00:00:14.730
whether it's in a play or like a movie.

00:00:14.730 --> 00:00:17.880
And the other sort of the symbolic idea

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:20.700
of what it means when
somebody makes a scene.

00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:24.570
And growing up in the South,
it wasn't considered ladylike.

00:00:24.570 --> 00:00:25.500
- Girl, I know.

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:27.420
I grew up there.
- Yeah.

00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:29.335
- But you know, the thing is
if you're an emotional person,

00:00:29.335 --> 00:00:30.168
like I was.

00:00:30.168 --> 00:00:31.260
(Kelly blows raspberry)

00:00:31.260 --> 00:00:33.240
Yeah, repressed feelings don't go away

00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:35.040
just because you will them too.

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:37.080
They're inevitably gonna come out.

00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:38.070
- Yeah.
- In another way.

00:00:38.070 --> 00:00:41.910
And I think there was like
this big fiasco on Twitter

00:00:41.910 --> 00:00:45.510
'cause I said some very
negative things about a show

00:00:45.510 --> 00:00:49.320
that I truly loved being on,
but it was within the context

00:00:49.320 --> 00:00:52.020
of being sexually harassed on that show.

00:00:52.020 --> 00:00:53.490
- Oh.
- Being intimidated,

00:00:53.490 --> 00:00:54.810
being controlled,

00:00:54.810 --> 00:00:58.050
and me wanting to swallow
that and hide that

00:00:58.050 --> 00:01:00.300
so I didn't stain the reputation

00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:02.880
of the only Asian-American
networks that come.

00:01:02.880 --> 00:01:05.640
- Do you feel obligated to say something?

00:01:05.640 --> 00:01:06.690
Do you react ever?

00:01:06.690 --> 00:01:08.100
Like, you know what I'm saying?

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:10.830
- Well, I mean, there was
definitely a social media pile on

00:01:10.830 --> 00:01:13.230
which I understood because
if you don't know me,

00:01:13.230 --> 00:01:15.420
it just looks like, "Oh,
she had this huge hit movie

00:01:15.420 --> 00:01:18.270
and now she thinks she's
outgrown the show,"

00:01:18.270 --> 00:01:19.103
which wasn't-

00:01:19.103 --> 00:01:20.820
- Yeah, but you led
with you don't know me.

00:01:20.820 --> 00:01:21.990
Which is they don't know you though.

00:01:21.990 --> 00:01:24.480
- Yeah, but it's easy to
think you know a public figure

00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:25.530
based on-
- Yeah.

00:01:25.530 --> 00:01:28.290
- The limited information
that you have of them.

00:01:28.290 --> 00:01:30.927
It's easy to construct that narrative.

00:01:30.927 --> 00:01:34.980
But I had been a public
figure for a while then,

00:01:34.980 --> 00:01:38.130
so I thought I was pretty
strong and pretty capable.

00:01:38.130 --> 00:01:39.660
But it was actually a few DMs

00:01:39.660 --> 00:01:43.050
from a former colleague
of mine, an Asian actress

00:01:43.050 --> 00:01:46.443
who you think she'd be on your side.

00:01:47.460 --> 00:01:51.030
That sort of convinced me that
life, my life was worthless.

00:01:51.030 --> 00:01:53.400
And I ended up in the hospital

00:01:53.400 --> 00:01:56.207
because I tried to take my own
life, which was really scary.

00:01:56.207 --> 00:01:57.810
- Yeah.

00:01:57.810 --> 00:01:59.880
- But ultimately, it was a good thing

00:01:59.880 --> 00:02:02.700
because it made me seek help.

00:02:02.700 --> 00:02:03.533
- Yeah.
- And I wouldn't

00:02:03.533 --> 00:02:05.400
have been able to talk
about it three years ago,

00:02:05.400 --> 00:02:08.430
because I was still very
like raw and wounded.

00:02:08.430 --> 00:02:09.263
- Yeah.
- But I think

00:02:09.263 --> 00:02:12.390
the thing I've learned now is
that through a lot of therapy

00:02:12.390 --> 00:02:16.833
and looking at what my values truly are,

00:02:17.790 --> 00:02:20.130
I've developed the tools to handle it.

00:02:20.130 --> 00:02:20.963
- Yeah.
- And so,

00:02:20.963 --> 00:02:23.370
I wanna talk about it so other young women

00:02:23.370 --> 00:02:25.290
who might be struggling
with the same thing

00:02:25.290 --> 00:02:26.340
know they're not alone

00:02:26.340 --> 00:02:28.440
and that there is a light
at the end of the tunnel.

00:02:28.440 --> 00:02:29.749
It takes work.
- Yeah.

00:02:29.749 --> 00:02:31.245
Work.
- But you can get there.

